#Why build a package? 
- Makes code easier to reuse 
- to avoid lots of copying and pasting
- to keep your functions up to date 
- to give your code to others. 

Course Content: 
- File Layout 
- Import structure 
- Making your packages installable 
- Adding liscenses and README's 
- Style and unit tests for a high quality package 
- Registering and publishing your package to PyPi 
- Using packaging templates. 

-- Scripts, Modules and packages. 
- Script: A python file which is run (python myscript.py)
- Package: A directroy full of python code to be imported (i.e. numpy) 
- Subpackage - A smaller package inside a package (e.g. numpy.random)
- Module - A python file inside a package which stores the package code. 
- Library - either a package, or collection of packages (e.g. the Python standard library (math, os, datetime))

